  "query_span_absolute": {
    "start": 44,
    "end": 183,
    "text": "About 3 years ago or so I was skinny, but I was still ugly. I really do want to change that but I've tried 3 times. Now can I try but don't stop. At school I get bullied about my weight and my ugliness and I have been bullied my whole life that I believe them. How can I stop thinking about them and don't let it get in my head? My parents said I don't weight that much but, they do think I am fat but, they tell me I am not. I told my parents that I need to go to a therapist, but they think I am fine and I think they don't want to deal with it."
  },
  "reasoning_spans": [
    {
      "id": "S1",
      "start": 2,
      "end": 18,
      "text": "Okay, the user is dealing with body image issues, bullying, and family dynamics."
    },
    {
      "id": "S2",
      "start": 19,
      "end": 33,
      "text": "They've tried dieting three times and now want to continue without stopping."
    },
    {
      "id": "S3",
      "start": 34,
      "end": 51,
      "text": "They feel bullied at school and believe the bullies, which is affecting their self-esteem."
    },
    {
      "id": "S4",
      "start": 52,
      "end": 71,
      "text": "Their parents are conflicted—saying they don't weigh much but also think they're fat."
    },
    {
      "id": "S5",
      "start": 72,
      "end": 95,
      "text": "The user wants to stop negative thoughts and not let them affect them, but their parents don't want to seek therapy."
    },
    {
      "id": "S6",
      "start": 96,
      "end": 104,
      "text": "First, I need to validate their feelings."
    },
    {
      "id": "S7",
      "start": 105,
      "end": 120,
      "text": "It's important to acknowledge the pain of bullying and the impact on self-esteem."
    },
    {
      "id": "S8",
      "start": 121,
      "end": 135,
      "text": "They might feel isolated, so emphasizing that they're not alone is key."
    },
    {
      "id": "S9",
      "start": 136,
      "end": 143,
      "text": "Then, address the body image issue."
    },
    {
      "id": "S10",
      "start": 144,
      "end": 161,
      "text": "They've tried dieting, which might have led to cycles of restriction and bingeing."
    },
    {
      "id": "S11",
      "start": 162,
      "end": 184,
      "text": "It's crucial to mention that weight loss isn't the solution and that self-worth isn't tied to appearance."
    },
    {
      "id": "S12",
      "start": 185,
      "end": 190,
      "text": "Next, the bullying."
    },
    {
      "id": "S13",
      "start": 191,
      "end": 209,
      "text": "They need strategies to cope, like focusing on positive aspects, setting boundaries, and seeking support."
    },
    {
      "id": "S14",
      "start": 210,
      "end": 219,
      "text": "Maybe suggest talking to a trusted teacher or counselor."
    },
    {
      "id": "S15",
      "start": 220,
      "end": 229,
      "text": "The parents' resistance to therapy is a barrier."
    },
    {
      "id": "S16",
      "start": 230,
      "end": 251,
      "text": "It's important to explain that therapy isn't just for \"problems\" but for building resilience and coping skills."
    },
    {
      "id": "S17",
      "start": 252,
      "end": 264,
      "text": "Also, they might be struggling with self-acceptance."
    },
    {
      "id": "S18",
      "start": 265,
      "end": 278,
      "text": "Encouraging self-compassion and challenging negative thoughts could help."
    },
    {
      "id": "S19",
      "start": 279,
      "end": 290,
      "text": "Maybe suggest activities that build confidence, like hobbies or sports."
    },
    {
      "id": "S20",
      "start": 291,
      "end": 306,
      "text": "They need to know it's okay to seek help and that they deserve support."
    },
    {
      "id": "S21",
      "start": 307,
      "end": 319,
      "text": "I should avoid giving medical advice and focus on emotional support."
    },
    {
      "id": "S22",
      "start": 320,
      "end": 336,
      "text": "Make sure the response is empathetic, non-judgmental, and practical."
    },
    {
      "id": "S23",
      "start": 337,
      "end": 348,
      "text": "Check for any harmful thoughts and ensure the advice is safe."
    },
    {
      "id": "S24",
      "start": 349,
      "end": 365,
      "text": "Finally, offer to help them find resources or support if they're open to it."
    }
  ],
